GPL software installed beside this MIT service
=============================================

The nc-performer kit and the nc-perform service are MIT, Copyright (c) 2026
Peter Semmelhack. See the LICENSE file at the root of the repository.

The container image also installs two separate programs so the default reverb
hack can run. They are not part of the MIT code. The kit calls them as
external tools. If they are missing, the reverb hack falls back to the
synthetic hall and the record says so.

1. Dragonfly Reverb (Dragonfly Hall), GPL-3.0
   https://github.com/michaelwillis/dragonfly-reverb
   Installed from the Debian package dragonfly-reverb in the image.

2. pedalboard, GPL-3.0
   https://github.com/spotify/pedalboard
   Installed from PyPI as pedalboard==0.9.26

Source for those programs is the upstream repositories above, at the versions
named here. If you received a binary image of nc-perform and want that
source, ask the person who gave you the image. They can point you at those
repositories and at the Debian package version used to build the image.
